body:
APPROVE — independent primary-source and status-model review of docs/design/movie-component-admission-ledger.md for bd-01M188P265MZVEKBD5BBN34E6T, documentation-only B0 component-ledger leg.

Status model:
- all named registry rows have explicit values on selection, rights/access, scientific role, operational posture, and realization; no blank/pending value or favorable inference from Unknown;
- Conditional is used only for nominated components whose exact code/policy leaf is PaperworkAdmitted while runtime/codec/native closure remains HoldUnknown;
- LocalRecipe + RecipeOnly does not imply configured, built, installed, run, reproduced, or remotely callable;
- Held is the first-court disposition, not a sixth component axis, and the text keeps that distinction clear;
- umbrella code/package/source licenses cannot flow to weights, transitive wheels, containers, codecs, services, benchmark annotations, or participant material.

FFmpeg primary checks:
- official release page confirms 9.0.1 Lei, 2026-08-12, release-signing fingerprint FCF986EA15E6E293A5644F10B4322F04D67658D8, tar/signature links, and verification procedure;
- live tag refs match annotated object 501bb49457b9dfb25d6a208832e0a6e6cd53108d and peeled bf1b838f2ab88b4f8fd83443325c782ea0e0f7fa;
- tagged LICENSE.md supports LGPL-2.1+, GPL activation by --enable-gpl, v3 activation by --enable-version3, GPL impact of libx264/libx265, and unredistributable --enable-nonfree builds;
- tagged configure supports the recorded disabling/enabling surface. The document correctly labels the command a candidate recipe, keeps source tarball/signature verification and native/codec/patent closure Unknown, and withholds every decoder pending F0/F1 manifests.

PySceneDetect primary checks:
- v0.7.1 tag resolves to 6ebb72392de8acfb6c539bf15d0aa912ce7ab6b2;
- PyPI attests both recorded SHA-256 values via Trusted Publishing from that exact tag;
- tagged BSD-3-Clause, Python >=3.10, Click constraint, unbounded NumPy/OpenCV-headless/Platformdirs/tqdm, and scenedetect-core reversal all match upstream;
- the direct detector API consumes sequential 24-bit BGR frames; ContentDetector has declared threshold/minimum length/component weights/luma/kernel/filter parameters and no learned artifact. The ledger correctly forbids high-level decode/time authority and holds preprocessing, dependency, container, and native closure.

No component was downloaded or executed; no gated terms or owner actions were touched. This review closes only the independently reviewed component-ledger documentation condition. The first court remains Held, and source admission, fixture manifests, two-run timebase repair, owner actions, P1, realization, installation, execution, and implementation authorization remain open and separate.
